    "text": "By David Kesiena ,\n7 hours ago Central Texas is heading into its heaviest rain of the week. The National Weather Service has a Flood Watch in effect through early Friday evening. Forecasters say the flash flooding risk peaks between 9 p.m. today and 6 a.m. Friday, when slow-moving storms along the I-35 corridor could drop 3 to more than 7 inches of rain in spots, depending on where the cells settle. Read full article",
